        <p>AUDITORS. COOPER BROTHERS and Co., Chartered Accountants, 14. George-street Mansion House, London. HARRY YIGiN, Chartered ile,aoantant. Toronto, Canada. HEOISTESED Ottetoss. 39, VICTOKIA-sTREIST.WBSTMIN- srmit. LONDON. S W. Yiworla Hines, Ontario, Canada, SERF.TART.—ROBIIRT MATHIAS. PROSPE TIJS.</p>
        <p>l This Company has been formed to carry on the business Of Mining and Smelting Nickel and Copper Ores, and of refining them by the patent process of Dr Ludwig Mond, F.R.S , which has been prooounced by the hi chest authorities an entirely new departure in metallurgy, and which, it is ex- pected will secure to this Company the command of the nickel trade. This invention utilises the remarkable and unicre property of nickel of forming a volati e compound with carbonic °side, Which was discovered by Dr. Mond and his collaborators some years ago This compound is produned at oroinary temperature from the matte obtained by smelting and Bosse- merislng nickel copper ores Star a simple preliminary treatment. On applying moderate heat, pure metallic nickel is obtained in a readily saleable form. Thus a metal of great purity la obtained from nickel ores of any kind at a small expenditure of labour, fuel, and other material as the carbonic oxide is used over and over again. This process has been fuly worked out in all details on a manufacturing scale at small works at Smathwick.where over 60 tons of wicket have been manufactured and delivered to a number of large consumers, trom whom very satisfactory reports were received as to Its corny. the copper in the matte is obtained as a bye product of the process In a most,valuable form, via,, as crystalised sulphite of IlOpper. Special machinery essential to the successful working of the process has been invented and protected by separate patents of recent date. 'the Company will acquire from Dr. Mond, under the con- tract mentioned hereafter, the whole of the Nickel business now carried on by him as a going cone- rn in Canada, Wales, and elsewhere in Great Britain, and all property ani assets belonging thereto (except cash in hams and at Bankers' In lino/land and Wales), as on and from first day of January, 1911, and the benefit and advantages of all Contracts as on and from that date (subject. however, as on and from the same date to all tbe liabilities relating to such business and under such Contracts). and in particular I. All let ers pat nt, bevels d'lnventiOn, privileges. Sm., granted to him, and which may be granted to him in the future relating to the extraction of nickel and to cognate 2. Freehold and Leasehold Nickel and Copper /dines in Ontario. Canada. 3. A freehold property of about 33 acres at Oirlach, near Swansea. where works for the production of nickel and of copper sulphate are being erectai. and certain leasehold lands and buildings, and a small plant now at Smethwick, near Birmingham. . . .</p>
        <p>--ii.ri;;;;,7.770. in number (see Appendix), have been granted to Dr. Mond in 25 countries, comprising every . conntry of induitrial Importance, including the United kingdom. Germany. United otates,and Canada. Dr. Mond's prone., is so novel that all patents were granted without the slightest difllmlty A number of the esseatial patens assure to the Company the leial monopoly of the process for terms yar,frig from nine to twelve years in the different cm-tries. The practical monopoly however, is not limited by the, duration of the patents, because the process requires intimate knowledg• of details for soccesifill working. The mining properties (see Appendix), which have bell fully reported upon by Mr Thomas Haight Leggett and Dr Bernturd Mohr, are at .unte in the townehms of 81.,aard. Damon, and Denison, in the Sudbury District of Ontario, Oanada. which dist, ict produces nearly half of the world's sup Ay of nickel. They compriie 22 mining location. cover- ing "Lout 49)0 acres, 335) of which are held freehold, and the balance under three years' lease with option of purchase. Nickel copper ore of good quality has up to now been proved by prospecting and diamond drilling on ten of these locations, and txtending m ire particularly in (*arson and Denison over a very considerable area. Vine of these miuln r locations are situated in Bleaard and Carson, and thirteen in Denivon. The latter, comprising about 23 ,Oacres freehold, are now known as the Victols Mines, and adjoin the railw ttation of that n ,me on the Canadian Pacift) hallway, 21 mdes west of Sudbury. On one of Ike thirteen legations in Denison. a mine known as the Victoria Mne No. I bas been developed by four shafts- The main shaft, being a three-compar..rnent winding shaft, has been completed to a depth of 210 feet Three levels of a total length of 620 feet have been driven at a cl,mh of 00, 120, and 20. i feet respe,tively. By these shafts and levels and by numerous diamond drill holes a very largo ore body has been proved to a depth of 210 feet. which in all proba.-dlity will extend to much greater depth. This mine Ti now In complete wmking order, and, according toll,. regular weekly returns forward,d by the Manager, me has been raised regularly since ihe beginning of Fehroarf, and has been transported by an aerial tramway to the -Itoastyarde, where, on the let instant. about 10,001 tons bad been delivered. 'The average essay of this ore is 3i per cent, of nickel end 31 per cent. of co: per. _ _</p>
        <p>Plant a the ino.t modem tyre for Boasting. finaelting„ and Besseinerislng this ore tms he-n erected at Victoria Mines, and is practical ready for sta,Ung under the direction of one of the hat known Metallinwists of the United States, Mr Hiram Hilton, lately of the iknacmdia Company who is superintending the Mining and Smelting operations in I Canada.</p>
        <p>SubAsntial ofticps and well-constrmterl houses for the accommodation of the staff, workmen and their families. aleo oinb-houses. Zze , h.tveteen ertv•ted, whcli fo.m quite an int. portant villa.e near Victoria Mines Station. A timb.r licerwe obtained by Dr Mon I from DIP Ont.rlo Government, covering a large area round Victoria Mines, I which the Compiny will acquire. will supply the mines and 'Works for many years with timber and fuel. Tbe Beesemerlaed Matte, produced by the smelting works</p>
