      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-05-17_WidnesExaminer_art0051" n="art0051">
        <head>:fIIODLIAR ACCIDENT.</head>
        <p>:fIIODLIAR ACCIDENT.</p>
        <p>Ab.itr. 11 3f/ en Thureday morninr, the plate glue window of t ie G orge and Dragon Hotel, Egerton- street, wit+ hrokan in a very peculiar manner. Lawrence Biil twin, a rag-g ,ther-r. of Haydock- stmt., Warring on, when gm g up the street was attacatd by the landlord'a .:og, whereupon be picked up a stens and threw it at he animal. The stone bounded on to the pavement, and into the winciow causing the damage. Mr Pater Riley (the lan 110 M) came outside to see the caw° of the crash and naturally had a little difference; but, we believe, landlord ant ragman. eventually squared their difference. RIVAL CHEIROLL PAVINTS.</p>
        <p>In the Ch swell [kyles in, on. Tbur-day morning, Mr Justice Buck'ey gave juigment in the action of Atkins and ppiegarch v. the Castner-lieliner A'ksli Company, in which the plain iffvelainsed an injun;:tiou to restrain the defendants fekim infring- ing their pa,ent for an improved apparistn4 for separating alk.,linn and earthy metals and other products from the salts of such metals, and other substances Contained therein. His‘lordship, in the cour-e of a lengthy judgment, said he tailed to find in the procas- which the plaint Ma claimed any new invention which was not found in previous 1 processes. Ile further considered that the plaintiff; patent failed as regard-d u iliry, and on the ques- tion of infringement he held that the defeniants'l appa, atus was essentially different, and that they' had no, infringed. On all the pAtits he gave ment,f 1' the d-fend,nts, and di missed with costs.' _</p>
