      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-05-17_WidnesExaminer_art0061" n="art0061">
        <head>LANDMARK ALREADY.</head>
        <p>A LANDMARK ALREADY.</p>
        <p>The year 1901 has already become a land maik in the n history of the United Kingdom, and sorrow bas marked.; with unwonted universality the whole of the n a-ions of I the Earth. How true is it, that grief and afil tion are the common lot of ad, nod that suffering c num to all I men and women alike, the great and the lowly, in the palace and in the cottage; but in sickness there is the sonsolation that suffering may be managed, strength increased, and health—generally speaking—restored by attention to the dictates of Nature, acd the enlistment in man's service of the bountiful goodness that abounds in the fertiity of the earth, the gifts of a beneficent pro- vidence. The most striking instance of the gathering in of these benefits for human suffering is found in Gwilym Evans Maine Bitters, which comprises a scientific , Compounding of the virtues to be derived from Saraap.r- illa Gentian, Burdock, Lavender, Dandelion, Saffron,l Sala Quinine: an army of health giving tonic properties lot to be surpassed. evcn in Nature's Garnery of Good- ness. This reviving, invigorating,strengthenlog remedy, when other attempts to cure have failed, often brings quick relief to sufferers from weakness of body, and un- strung nerves, indigestion, poor blood,depressed spirits. and it increases the joy of life to all. I:: well may be Seemed " Nature's Great Tonic." - -</p>
