      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-05-17_WidnesExaminer_art0063" n="art0063">
        <head>BEFORE the MAGISTRATES</head>
        <p>BEFORE the MAGISTRATES</p>
        <p>feaereemas Cass OF CHILD Neenece.—" A Bea or Boars."—CONDEeesieD MILS AS FOOD FOR BARTEL YesterdaV'at the Warrioeten Felice C urt before ti c 'Mayor and a full benclieldary Jane F.neh,a young woman of respectable appearance,residing at 69 Knut s ford.read, Nirte3 stionnetred at the instance c f the N S.P.C.C. fer nee/letting tier illegitimate child. Cyril Wright Finch, Annie Percival, 10, Gendyeayard, woo had bad charge rel the child was alio charged with neglecting it.—Me A Browee appeared on behalf of the Society and said the case was rather out of the ordinary run of suet oases. The child in question was 111 months old and the negtect complained of was unereper and negligent feeding, the result of which was that instead of being the nominal weight of 17ins. the ' child only weighed 1011 as 4 ounces. The fleet a. f mdent ' WAS the mother of the child and the second deferelant ' was her aunt. Mrs Percival agreed to keep the team I f? 34 a week. The firs: defendant kept up the pm meats of 3s let some time, but for ttie last few months rho had ant gent anything except one or two tins of cin eased milk. It would be stated by doctors that condensed milk, especially of the borne that defendant purchased, Was not proper food for a baby. S .metimes the beby had only one tin per week. He (Mr Browne) was in a difficulty bemuse the Act of Parliament seal the perion who had the custedy of the child ehould be liable tor the nrglect. Be believed Mrs Percival did attend to the child until her husband ded some time ago. She was sow dependent upon her a .na for maiuteerince and they paid her something like 20s per week. At the same time she should not have neglected the child. Ha was afraid diet under the circumstances they a mile not be able to obtain a conviction against her and be would withdraw the CUP against her and proceed against Atm el:other. D-lendsnt was a clerk at Mr Mortonts electekted works and earned Se per week. The child had been taken back to her sever