      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-05-17_WidnesExaminer_art0100" n="art0100">
        <head>Seven Inmates Burnt to Death.</head>
        <p>Seven Inmates Burnt to Death.</p>
        <p>A Stafford clrrespondent telegraphs :—A fire, by whieh s •ven lives were Inet, broke out on Thursday morning ab Ar. two o'clock, at the S'eaff rd Work- house. The lire occurred In the old infirmary, which was occupied by eleven persons, inclaaiug the workhouse cook.</p>
        <p>Six of the bodies were found lying on the floor, and they presented a sickening appearance. They wars badly charred, but death was apparently due to suff ication. Ole of them had attempted to escape, and h-ad got as far as the door, when he was overpowered. Toe body of ths cook was forted lying partially dressed upon her bed. Otte of the men who escaped jampe I twenty feet from a win- dow, and alighted aortae:, and six inohsciles, who occupied another room, were rescued by means of ladders.</p>
