      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-05-17_WidnesExaminer_art0112" n="art0112">
        <head>RUNCORN FOOTBALL CLUB. --- Nominations for 1901-02.</head>
        <p>RUNCORN FOOTBALL CLUB. --- Nominations for 1901-02.</p>
        <p>- - Mr A LiAltburn pro Oded over a special meoling of the memb've of the Runro'n Fortball Club, held for the purpose of r.c 4ving the nominations 'for the severat f&gt;ffiles of the c' b for the ensuing season, at Mr /ales Café, Bridge-street. During the evening the following nominations were received :—President, Mr Stenuel Taylor, JP, 11;•dal Mount; Treasurer, C Pownell, Victoria-road ; Secretary, Mr J Eli,, 13, Bluth Bank.terrane ; Assistant secretary, Mr A Abel,22, Byron-street ; Committee, Messrs W J .nes,A Lightburn. 11 Wright, JF Moulton. fi Cairley, P D Alpo, T Rabb:- ann. G. Robin.nn, W Faulkner, A Abel, R Garnett, S Adams, fl N Linaker, FT Gr-nods, F Bann-Ink, J Widdows, W C Brirnelow, D Lightfoq, 0 Wainwright. WE Dudley, 3 H Weston, 8 Hardy, 0- Luston. Hughes and 0 Mackie. The first named twelve were the members of the retiring co nmittee. Au.litors : Messrs T C Cooper, and E Limb ; captain Rni vice- captain of first team, Messrs 3 Illuntcn,J Butterworth , anl 3 Flulkz:er : captain and vice-captain of second I team, Messrs J Nickron, J Morran, W Betrtev and II Joie. Me annual general meeting will he held in the Bethesda Schoilroom. Runcorn. on Tuesday next, at 7,30 p.m. prompt.</p>
