        <p>• Detailed ratements are gavel! hi the report of the club"a record during the season with the , individual scorere in the Brea and A ream% It appears that there were 47 committee meetings, and the attendances are ,follow itahtori 41, 1' P-mberton 46,W Hewitt 45, T Thnrmilec 41 W D.Io 29, T Bowers 411, T Barnes 46, W li,vins 46 RON. TREASURER'S REPORT. Mr T PIIMBERT N (..au aeureaary) says :—The semen jest elide i 1144 new, is very eventful one in the history of the club. T. begi.. with, the annual spans which should have b-en held on the Bank Holiday in August Last had to be post p,,,ed owing to the wretched weather which prevailed on that day and in consequence the receipts at the gate at the postponed meeting were moth leia and the B'4 greoter, the profit being £3B 0. 81 against £lO2 84 81 in the previous Fear. Tho ciao has been fortuoate to earn the sum of £53 154 61 frcm the trips to L -eds asd Manchester, but Mil is an item whinh cannot al ways be depended upon, The I,tt,aidanc a, the football matches has been very good, and has resulted in a iaro increase in the receipts at the gate The committee decided to go on with the South West Loneashire Competition for another season, but re i her financially nor otherwise has this proved of any nenek. The gates a, Warriegton real,zed £lll 2a 91 for the it round and a, ay-final and en you will see by the acceunts we have received £29 6s 9d. The neat was played ar Wi,o.an end I have not y.. I and whether ill 7 shall receive any portion of the r.aleipts.lEhe receipts durine the imp ties away from home were disappoint- ing. In the fist hound at Leeds oscine to the storm the total rec Opts only suilunt, dto £ll3 124. In the corns- fiat against Cabtleforl our sb •re was £55 4s 81. nut of the gross takinvr of £224 15.31. In Ito final at Leeds where the tic ird f " gates " was established, the Union granted the club the sum of £5O. T e expenOi- tore of Choi club has been kept down as far as possible, bat as I predie